1
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,090
Hello.

2
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:19,470
Hello.

3
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:21,270
I love my new job!

4
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,270
Honey, you're screaming.

5
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,270
You bet your ass I am.

6
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:26,400
I just had the best first day ever.

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,730
The kitchen? Twice as big as Allessandro's.

8
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,730
Oh, that's great.

9
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,730
Yeah.

10
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:35,200
And clean? Not just Health Department-clean, Monica-clean.

11
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:36,950
Awesome.

12
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:39,280
Oh, and the people are so nice.

13
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:41,950
There's this one guy, Jeffrey, he's the maitred.

14
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:44,290
Chandler, you will love him.

15
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:47,250
He is without a doubt the funniest guy I have ever met.

16
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,220
This is nice.

17
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,220
I know.

18
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:57,110
You need both hands for that?

19
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:57,110
Yeah, I kind of do.

20
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,320
Well, how's this?

21
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:16,710
Oh, look at you two holding hands.

22
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:18,970
Is this getting serious?

23
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,680
Well, I, you know...

24
00:02:20,970 --> 00:02:22,970
Have you not talked about it yet?

25
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:26,720
Am I making you uncomfortable?

26
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,890
If you were bigger you'd hit me, huh?

27
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,030
I'm sorry, heh.

28
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:41,110
It's obviously way too early for us to be having that conversation.

29
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:43,200
Is it?

30
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:43,200
Maybe not. Is it?

31
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:45,200
Okay, when I got divorced...

32
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:48,570
I didn't think I'd feel this way about someone for a really long time.

33
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,500
Then again, I didn't think I'd meet someone like you.

34
00:02:52,830 --> 00:02:56,040
And this may be crazy-soon, but I want you to have this.

35
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,260
No, not... That's gum.

36
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,260
Oh.

37
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:04,850
Oh, five bucks. I love it when that happens, you know?

38
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:07,470
You don't know it's there...

39
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:07,470
I know. Keep digging.

40
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:08,970
Oh, sorry.

41
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,560
Oh. It's a key.

42
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:18,110
To be honest, I think I'd prefer the five dollars.

43
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,700
It's to my apartment.

44
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,700
Oh, wow.

45
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,190
Ooh. Big step for Phoebe and Mike.

46
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:27,740
Look, I don't want you to feel like you have to give me your key...

47
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,660
No, I want to.

48
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,660
Oh, thank God.

49
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,960
Yeah.

50
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:36,080
Wow. I was starting to think I'd never meet someone that...

51
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,750
you know, I wanted to do this with.

52
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:41,300
Here you go.

53
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:45,180
This is cool, huh?

54
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:45,180
It really is.

55
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:51,060
Oh, I know it. It is amazing. These little things open doors.

56
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:57,020
So I don't go back to work for another four weeks...

57
00:03:57,190 --> 00:03:59,230
but we would like our nanny to start right away...

58
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:01,240
so that Emma could get a chance to know her.

59
00:04:01,610 --> 00:04:03,570
I think that's really smart.

60
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:06,110
The easier we can make the transition for her the better.

61
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,320
That's great. Great.

62
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:09,870
So do you have any questions for us?

63
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:09,870
Not really.

64
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,370
All right. Well, thank you so much for coming.

65
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:15,120
Thank you.

66
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:15,120
It was really nice to meet you.

67
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:17,790
We will call you.

68
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:17,790
Oh, you know, wait.

69
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,670
I do have one question.

70
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,670
Yeah.

71
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,800
Do you guys do random drug testing?

72
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:27,800
Boy, we, uh, hadn't really thought of that.

73
00:04:27,970 --> 00:04:31,930
That's cool. But if you do, I'm gonna need three days' notice.

74
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,560
Okey-dokey.

75
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:36,800
Wow. We're never gonna find a nanny.

76
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:40,520
Come on, Rach. We will. I promise. We have more interviews.

77
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:44,820
And worse comes to worst, we can always reconsider the, uh, first one we met with.

78
00:04:45,070 --> 00:04:47,350
What, the blond with no bra?

79
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:48,780
She was blond?

80
00:04:51,370 --> 00:04:52,410
Just a sec.

81
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:55,790
Okay, this one's name is Sandy.

82
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:55,790
Okay.

83
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:59,210
She's got a degree in Early Childhood Education.

84
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:03,210
Uh, she worked for her last family for three years.

85
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:04,760
Okay.

86
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:09,090
Hi. I'm Sandy.

87
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:14,980
And she's a little mannish.

88
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,060
Ah! Oh, my God. David.

89
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,060
Hi.

90
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:29,530
Uh, is this a bad time?

91
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:29,530
No, it's a great time. Come in.

92
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:31,830
Wow. Hi.

93
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:35,200
Oh, my gosh. What are you doing here? Are you back from Minsk?

94
00:05:35,370 --> 00:05:37,040
Well, just for a couple of days.

95
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,790
I'm here to explain to the people who gave us our grant...

96
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,750
why it's a positive thing that we've spent all their money...

97
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,210
and, uh, accomplished, uh, nothing.

98
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,720
Who cares? It got you here.

99
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:52,050
Well, it got me to New York anyway. Then I got in a cab at the airport...

100
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:53,890
and the guy said, "Where to?"

101
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:57,850
I just gave him your address. I didn't even think about it.

102
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,360
Wow. Where's your luggage?

103
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,820
Damn it.

104
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,400
All right, I'll call the cab company.

105
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:12,660
We can call them later. Can you just stand there for a moment?

106
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,290
Boy.

107
00:06:16,450 --> 00:06:19,290
There's an old Russian expression, um, that goes:

108
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,460
Roughly translated, that means, um

109
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:28,880
"This thing that I'm looking at: Wow."

110
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:32,430
Thank you.

111
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:36,180
Uh, no, you should see me when... Actually, no, I look pretty good.

112
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:38,770
Are you kidding?

113
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:41,230
You know, when you don't see someone for a long time...

114
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,980
and you kind of build them up in your head, you start thinking:

115
00:06:44,150 --> 00:06:47,150
"Come on, don't be crazy, nobody's that beautiful."

116
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,820
But, well, you are.

117
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:54,780
Well, so, um, are you seeing anyone?

118
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:57,870
No.

119
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:01,580
I'm just the worst person ever.

120
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:04,330
How can I not tell David that I'm seeing Mike?

121
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:06,130
Maybe he didn't give you a chance.

122
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:09,760
He said, "Are you seeing someone?" And I said, "No."

123
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:13,720
Oh, well, that would've been your window.

124
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:13,720
Yeah.

125
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:17,640
I mean, I don't know. I was looking in his eyes...

126
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:21,390
and I was just thinking, "Oh, my God, it's David. David's here."

127
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,980
He's just so irresistible.

128
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,480
Really? The scientist guy?

129
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,480
Really? Chandler?

130
00:07:33,910 --> 00:07:35,660
Continue.

131
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,990
Okay, then it gets worse...

132
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:40,250
because I told him I would see him tomorrow night.

133
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:43,870
Phoebe.

134
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:43,870
I know. Evil.

135
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:45,960
And, and, and, and...

136
00:07:46,130 --> 00:07:51,550
I like Mike so much, you know? It's just going really well. Oh, my God.

137
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:54,090
Wow, isn't it ironic that David would show up...

138
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:56,760
on the same day that you and Mike exchange keys?

139
00:07:57,050 --> 00:07:59,220
Uh-huh.

140
00:07:59,430 --> 00:08:02,640
Yeah. You know, and given my lifelong search for irony...

141
00:08:02,810 --> 00:08:04,850
you can imagine how happy I am.

142
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:10,440
What are you gonna do?

143
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:10,440
I mean, I guess I just have to...

144
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:14,110
tell David that nothing can happen between us.

145
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,570
Unless I don't.

146
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:18,740
You know, complicated moral situation?

147
00:08:18,910 --> 00:08:21,580
No right, no wrong?

148
00:08:18,910 --> 00:08:21,580
You have to tell David.

149
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:25,540
I knew I should've had this conversation with Joey.

150
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:30,710
Funniest guy she's ever met.

151
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,960
I'm funny, right?

152
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:35,680
What do you know? You're a door.

153
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,600
You just like knock-knock jokes.

154
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,680
Save it for inside.

155
00:08:45,230 --> 00:08:46,520
Hey.

156
00:08:45,230 --> 00:08:46,520
Hey.

157
00:08:46,810 --> 00:08:51,480
So Oklahoma's a crazy place. You know, they call it the Sooner State.

158
00:08:51,650 --> 00:08:54,110
Frankly, I'd sooner be in any other state.

159
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:58,700
And what's with Oklahoma having a panhandle?

160
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:00,580
Can all states have stuff like that?

161
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:04,120
Hey, yeah, I'm from the, uh, waistband of Wyoming.

162
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:08,380
But when I was 7, we headed over to the crotch.

163
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,710
Was your cabin pressurized?

164
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:16,130
And don't get me started on the way the people from Tulsa talk.

165
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,090
Okay.

166
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:21,260
What's with the word "y'all"?

167
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:24,140
You know, just two words just pushed together?

168
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:27,560
Are we all allowed to do that? Because if so, I say why stop there?

169
00:09:27,730 --> 00:09:31,400
You know, your new poodle could be your noodle.

170
00:09:31,650 --> 00:09:34,280
And fried chicken could be fricken.

171
00:09:34,990 --> 00:09:37,360
Waiter? Waiter, excuse me, I'll have the fricken.

172
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:42,030
See, that's funny with the fricken, right?

173
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:46,700
No, it just reminds me of something this guy did today at work.

174
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:49,540
I told you about that funny guy, Jeffrey, right?

175
00:09:49,710 --> 00:09:51,130
Yeah, he came up.

176
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,300
Well, he did this bit. You probably had to be there...

177
00:09:56,470 --> 00:10:01,140
but it was Liza Minnelli locked in our freezer eating a raw chicken.

178
00:10:01,430 --> 00:10:02,850
Oh, ha, ha.

179
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:09,480
Were you there?

180
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:09,480
No, but it sounds fricken funny.

181
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:16,440
I really understand how hard it's gotta be to leave your child with another person.

182
00:10:16,610 --> 00:10:19,900
I mean, it's like leaving behind a piece of your heart.

183
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:24,240
Sandy, that's exactly what it is.

184
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:29,250
Are you gay?

185
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:29,250
Ross.

186
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:31,580
It's okay. I get that a lot doing what I do.

187
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:34,710
But I am straight. I'm engaged, actually.

188
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:34,710
Oh.

189
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:37,380
Her name's Delia.

190
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:37,380
That's pretty.

191
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:43,510
So you're just, like, a guy who's a nanny.

192
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:49,020
I realize how it's a bit unorthodox for some people.

193
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:53,230
But I really believe the most satisfying thing you can do with your life...

194
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,900
is take care of a child.

195
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,980
Okay.

196
00:10:59,650 --> 00:11:01,030
Like at my last job.

197
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,320
I met Daniel when he was 3 weeks old.

198
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:07,120
And I got to watch him grow into this awesome person.

199
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:10,410
When I left, I said, "I'll see you soon."

200
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:13,630
And he said to me, "Skadandy?"

201
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:18,050
That was his name for me.

202
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:18,050
Oh, ha, ha.

203
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:22,470
"I'll see you every day right in..."

204
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:32,730
It's okay.

205
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:32,730
Yeah, kids say all kinds of crap.

206
00:11:37,190 --> 00:11:39,440
Oh, God, she must need her diaper changed.

207
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:44,320
I can take care of that, if you want.

208
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:44,320
Oh, that would be great.

209
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:49,990
I love him, I love him, I love him.

210
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:52,250
Oh, come on. Rach, he's a guy.

211
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:54,710
So what? He's smart. He's qualified.

212
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,040
Give me one good reason we shouldn't try him out.

213
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,710
Because it's weird.

214
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,340
Why?

215
00:12:02,550 --> 00:12:05,010
What kind of a job is that for a man? A nanny?

216
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:08,260
I mean, it's like if a woman wanted to be...

217
00:12:08,430 --> 00:12:09,720
Yes?

218
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:13,480
King?

219
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:18,900
I, uh, hope you don't mind. I used some of my homemade lotion on Emma.

220
00:12:19,070 --> 00:12:23,190
It's a mixture of calendula and honey cream. It'll dry that rash right up.

221
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:26,490
Plus, it keeps the hands young.

222
00:12:33,290 --> 00:12:35,420
Yes. Sandy, you're hired.

223
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:37,670
That's great.

224
00:12:41,550 --> 00:12:42,630
I'm sorry.

225
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:46,260
It's just such an emotional thing when you're welcomed into a new family.

226
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:47,760
Oh, God. Come here.

227
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:53,810
You gotta be at least bi.

228
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:03,530
Hey.

229
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:14,080
I need you to set me up for a joke.

230
00:13:14,250 --> 00:13:16,710
When Monica's around, ask me about fire trucks.

231
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:21,880
Ooh, I don't know, Chandler. I'm not so good with remembering lines.

232
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:26,840
Well, thank God your livelihood doesn't depend on it.

233
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:28,840
I know, right?

234
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:31,350
Why are we doing this?

235
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:35,140
Monica says that her maitred' is the funniest guy she's ever met.

236
00:13:35,310 --> 00:13:37,240
Seriously? She actually said that?

237
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:39,310
Yes. Am I crazy to be this upset?

238
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:42,520
No. Being funny's your thing.

239
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:42,520
Yeah.

240
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:45,190
Without that, you just got "lame with women."

241
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:45,190
Yeah...

242
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:48,320
Hi. There you are.

243
00:13:48,490 --> 00:13:49,740
Fire trucks.

244
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:04,960
Wow. You look even more beautiful than you did yesterday.

245
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:09,090
Ooh.

246
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:09,090
In fact, I'm going to kiss you now.

247
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:12,350
Oh, wait, wait.

248
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:12,350
Yeah, I can't get away with stuff like that.

249
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:15,520
It sounded sexy in my head, so I...

250
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:17,890
No, no, it's not that.

251
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:23,310
Remember when you asked me if I was seeing someone and I said no?

252
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:29,990
Well, um, I am. His name's Mike.

253
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:29,990
Oh. Oh.

254
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:33,370
I should've told you.

255
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:33,370
No.

256
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:36,160
Well, yeah.

257
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:36,160
Yeah.

258
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:42,040
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

259
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:42,040
Well, it's okay. I understand.

260
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,750
Well, are you happy with this guy?

261
00:14:45,090 --> 00:14:47,050
I am happy.

262
00:14:45,090 --> 00:14:47,050
Damn it.

263
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:50,680
I'm sorry. I don't mean that. I want you to be happy.

264
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:54,140
