00:30:40,790 --> 00:30:42,130
Playing and learning.

526
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:50,630
And my father walks in and says, "What are you doing with those things?

527
00:30:50,840 --> 00:30:52,480
What's wrong with you?

528
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:56,770
Why aren't you outside playing like a real boy?"

529
00:30:57,060 --> 00:31:00,350
But you are a real boy.

530
00:30:57,060 --> 00:31:00,350
I know I am.

531
00:31:02,650 --> 00:31:07,780
And when it's summer and it's hot, why can't you wear a tank top?

532
00:31:09,150 --> 00:31:15,370
It's all right. Crying is good. It lets the boo-hoos out.

533
00:31:16,700 --> 00:31:18,870
Here comes some more.

534
00:31:27,420 --> 00:31:30,670
And what's the one kind of boat that can never ever sink?

535
00:31:30,970 --> 00:31:35,850
What kind?

536
00:31:30,970 --> 00:31:35,850
A friendship.

537
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:41,060
Wow. You blow my mind.

538
00:31:43,020 --> 00:31:45,060
Oh, I gotta go.

539
00:31:43,020 --> 00:31:45,060
Aw.

540
00:31:45,230 --> 00:31:47,020
How much do I owe you?

541
00:31:45,230 --> 00:31:47,020
Twenty bucks.

542
00:31:47,650 --> 00:31:50,690
It's like the cheapest college ever.

